  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 and takes about 40 minutes including marinating time."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chicken"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "karaage"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "is one of Japan's most popular home dishes. The chicken is juicy inside and deeply crunchy outside."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The double-fry is what sets this apart. Fry the chicken once at 160°C to cook it through. Let it rest for 3 minutes, then fry again at 180°C for 90 seconds. The second fry drives out moisture and creates the signature crunch."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "chicken-thigh",
              "amount": 700,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "boneless, skin on, cut into 4cm chunks",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "soy-sauce-light",
              "amount": 40,
